# Scene 5: split view. Reading's Arch Linux row (y = 278, above LWN's at y = 323) is
# dragged onto the LWN page on screen: once the pointer is over the page its left
# half lights in the Space's colour, with "Create split view", and the drop makes the
# split, Arch Linux on the left, LWN on the right (splits J10, J11). The address row
# then has a part in each pane's colour, Arch's dark grey over the left and white over
# LWN, blended over the gap (toolbar T41). The press that starts the drag selects the
# dragged row for a moment (J10); the page that was on screen comes back once the
# pointer is over the page. The drag leaves the sidebar level with the row, so the
# row does not pass LWN's and the list does not reorder on the way out. The dragmove
# takes 1.5 s and holds 0.5 s; the half stays lit about 1.5 s in all. The pointer
# then goes back to the sidebar's ground, off the pages' links.
shot @MARKS@/split.png
glide 150 278 0.5
dragstart 150 278
dragmove 600 292
wait 0.5
dragend
wait 1.0
glide 150 720 0.5
